<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		The highmate xenotype uses Better Gene Inheritance's recessive genes instead of VRE - Highmate's own recessive
		genome, so the same inheritance behaviour is not supplied twice under two names.
		This folder only loads when Better Gene Inheritance and VRE - Highmate are both active (see loadFolders.xml),
		so no FindMod checks are needed.

		Load order matters here, unlike most of these patches. Highmate is a vanilla Biotech xenotype and does not ship
		with VRE_RecessiveGenome; VRE - Highmate adds it with a patch of its own, in its 1.6/Patches/XenotypeDefs.xml.
		RimWorld applies patches in mod order, so this replacement only finds its target if this mod loads after VRE -
		Highmate. About.xml lists it under loadAfter for that reason. Do not remove that entry.

		Verified against the current 1.6 releases: BGI_RecessiveGenes exists in Better Gene Inheritance, and VRE -
		Highmate's patch puts VRE_RecessiveGenome on the highmate through both its match and nomatch branches, so the
		gene is there whichever branch runs.
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
		<xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="Highmate"]/genes/li[text()="VRE_RecessiveGenome"]</xpath>
		<value>
			<li>BGI_RecessiveGenes</li>
		</value>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
